cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the paper
  of the footprint model you used (e.g. Kljun et al. 2015,
  doi:10.5194/gmd-8-3695-2015 - each output's metadata records the model's
  citation and DOI).
title: FluxPrint
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Herig Coimbra
    given-names: Pedro Henrique
    email: pedro-henrique.herig-coimbra@inrae.fr
    affiliation: ECOSYS, INRAE, AgroParisTech, Universite Paris-Saclay
repository-code: https://github.com/pedrohenriquecoimbra/fluxprint
url: https://github.com/pedrohenriquecoimbra/fluxprint
abstract: >-
  Flux footprint models for eddy covariance data analysis, behind a single
  consistent interface: batch processing of half-hourly met tables, typed
  footprint objects, source-area contours, georeferencing and NetCDF/GeoTIFF/
  Shapefile export.
keywords:
  - flux footprint
  - eddy covariance
  - micrometeorology
license: EUPL-1.2
version: 0.3.0
